    "result_text": "The full suite is green (that single `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project). The build also succeeded, which confirms the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` now carries `namesakeCount` and MapStruct maps it cleanly.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same first and last name, case-insensitively \u2014 returned on the created owner and readable via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges, each kept in its natural place:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated DTO exposes it.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `namesakeCount` column with getter/setter (mapped automatically by the existing MapStruct `OwnerMapper`).\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column. The test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` with `hsqldb/schema.sql`, so this is what makes the column real at runtime.\n4. **`NamesakeCounter.java`** \u2014 a new small single-responsibility `@Component` (mirroring `CustomerCodeAssigner`/`HouseholdMatcher`) that counts already-stored owners whose first and last names match case-insensitively and assigns the count on the owner.\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 injected `NamesakeCounter` and called `assign(owner)` in the pre-save step chain, before `saveOwner`, so the count reflects owners stored before this create and never counts itself.\n\nThe count is computed once at creation time and persisted (rather than recomputed on read), which is required because it's defined relative to the moment of creation.",
